course: dictionary
lesson: 3144
title: Embankment: a raised bank
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An embankment is a long bank of earth or stone, built up above the land around it. It might carry a road or a railway, or stop a river from flooding the fields beside it. The clues are in the words around it: «Toad jumped, rolled down a short embankment» tells you it is a slope you can roll down.
explain: Toad was on the run, and he hid near the embankment. Ask yourself what word would fit: a bank or slope, raised up, not a hole. Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Some embankments are famous. The Thames Embankment is a raised walk and road beside the river in London. When context is not enough, a dictionary or a map will settle it.
fact: An embankment is a long bank of earth or stone built up above the land.
fact: Railway embankments carry train tracks above the fields around them.
fact: River embankments help stop the water from flooding the land beside the river.
fact: The Thames Embankment is a raised walk and road beside the river in London.
fact: Railway embankments are dangerous places to play, so always keep off them.
exercise: «Toad jumped, rolled down a short embankment, picked himself up unhurt.» What is an embankment? | A deep hole in the ground | A type of train ticket | *A long bank of earth or stone | A small river boat
exercise: Why do builders make a river embankment? | To hide the river from view | To keep fish in one place | *To stop the river flooding the land | To make the river run faster
exercise: In «Toad jumped, rolled down a short embankment», which word tells you the embankment was not big? | jumped | *short | rolled | embankment
test: Why are railway embankments dangerous places to play? | *Trains use them and the slopes are steep, so it is unsafe | They are too quiet to hear | They are warm in winter | They are made of soft cake
test: The Thames Embankment is in which city? | Paris | Sydney | Glasgow | *London
exam: Toad hid in the wood after rolling down an embankment. What is an embankment? | A kind of hat | *A long raised bank of earth or stone | A bunch of wild flowers | A cave in the hills
